Section 2.16.- Termination of an Employment Contract
The employment contract, except as otherwise provided in a special law, shall
be terminated:
(a) by a mutual agreement of the parties;
(b) on the grounds set forth in the contract;
(c) the expiration of the agreed on period or the completion of the work or
services object of the contract;
(d) the employee’s resignation or abandonment of the job;
(e) employee’s death or disability beyond the job holding period
established in a special law;
(f) employee’s retirement;
(g) a change of employer, unless there is an agreement between the parties
or a law that provides to the contrary;
(h) the employee’s discharge, or;
(i) noncompliance with the rules of conduct.
